{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>My punishment is greater than I can bear</b>. According to the opinion of all the commentators, he confessed his sin, and they interpret נשוא as meaning 'pardoned,' like נושא עון (Exodus 34:7). In my opinion, the Hebrews call the consequence and the evil punishment that comes on account of sin חטאת, and likewise 'for the punishment of the Amorite is not yet complete' (Genesis 15:16), 'if punishment comes upon you' (1 Samuel 28:10), 'and the punishment of the daughter of my people is magnified' (Lamentations 4:6). And the meaning is: this punishment is greater than I can endure. And the verse that follows it indicates the truth of this interpretation." "And the meaning of פצתה is 'opened,' like 'and Belial opens his mouth' (Job 35:16)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "The word עון appears throughout but refers to 'punishment' in Ibn Ezra's reading; the English 'punishment' is used to reflect his interpretation rather than the literal 'iniquity.'"}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:43:12.916869562Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}